; C++ (ECIL v1, slice S4): new[] and delete.  NEW_ARRAY_SIZE (overflow
; builtins, or, select; negative or overflowing counts give SIZE_MAX),
; NEW_ARRAY_COOKIE (the count at ptr + cookie - 8, the elements at ptr +
; cookie, also for an over-aligned element with a 16-byte cookie) and DELETE:
; cir.delete_array with its sized and aligned operator delete parameters, the
; destructor and operator delete calls of a single object, null checks, and
; an operator delete that takes the pointer only.  The program checks the
; sizes and pointers the operators receive and the destruction order.
; RUN: cat %S/Inputs/header08_cxx.txt %s > %t.txt
; RUN: %ecil-asm %t.txt -o %t.ecil
; RUN: %edg-cir --emit=cir %t.ecil | %FileCheck %s
; RUN: %edg-cir --emit=obj -o %t.o %t.ecil
; RUN: gcc %t.o -o %t.exe
; RUN: %t.exe

; CHECK-DAG: cir.mul.overflow
; CHECK-DAG: cir.add.overflow
; CHECK-DAG: cir.select
; CHECK-DAG: cir.delete_array {{.*}} delete_fn(@_ZdaPvm) delete_params<size = true{{.*}}> element_dtor(@_ZN1TD1Ev) element_align(4)
; CHECK-DAG: cir.delete_array {{.*}} delete_fn(@_ZdaPvmSt11align_val_t) delete_params<size = true, alignment = 16{{.*}}> element_dtor(@_ZN3A16D1Ev) element_align(16)
; CHECK-DAG: cir.array.ctor

